    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "a047e2a1-2dfd-3a66-b4e7-c0477ebf7d2c",
                "word": "matriotism",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "35381478-2b69-3006-a792-9730a6939dbe",
                        "entry_id": "a047e2a1-2dfd-3a66-b4e7-c0477ebf7d2c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "School, hometown, or parish pride or loyalty, as opposed to nationalism or patriotism."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f4a6174e-7bbb-4cd0-9e5b-20c5c07a2d9f",
                                "sense_id": "35381478-2b69-3006-a792-9730a6939dbe",
                                "text": "I am delighted with your ma'''triotism. \"Rome, Venice, Cambridge!\" I take it for an ascending scale, Rome being the first step and Cambridge the glowing apex."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "549b7dec-209c-41c7-964e-4ac0f66ee917",
                                "sense_id": "35381478-2b69-3006-a792-9730a6939dbe",
                                "text": "[The poem] \"Almae Matres\" celebrates \"a land of waters green and clear,\" and \"a little city worn and grey.\" […] But though Mr. [Andrew] Lang's matriotism is thus divided, he has only one fatherland [Scotland], and to that he is faithful against the world."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f9b5c4ef-ea21-3b16-bcf6-e49c0f8b1b77",
                        "entry_id": "a047e2a1-2dfd-3a66-b4e7-c0477ebf7d2c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The love or celebration of a woman's influence upon society; the female equivalent to male patriotism."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f499dfa4-4fa6-412e-93c5-30e1200b7698",
                                "sense_id": "f9b5c4ef-ea21-3b16-bcf6-e49c0f8b1b77",
                                "text": "Patriotism has incited men to live and die for the country and government; but Matriotism has impelled women to live and work for mankind. […] The Matriotism of household economics needs to be recognized as necessary for the whole of society."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8c63570b-b5a2-3b21-b64a-71ad5662e6e8",
                        "entry_id": "a047e2a1-2dfd-3a66-b4e7-c0477ebf7d2c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The love of the motherland, as opposed to patriotism as love of the fatherland."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c813df18-42ad-4bea-a408-26796f14e079",
                                "sense_id": "8c63570b-b5a2-3b21-b64a-71ad5662e6e8",
                                "text": "[page 225] The most extreme Russian patriots are matriots at heart. By this I mean that their devotion to \"Mother Russia\" is so intense that the underlying maternal fantasy basis of patriotism comes to the surface as maternal imagery, while paternal imagery fades away. […] [page 226] A true \"son of the Motherland\" does not distinguish his own interests from those of the Motherland. Indeed he is one with her. This is the meaning of matriotism: […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7f40aa4b-3091-3b80-a472-ad059412f890",
                        "entry_id": "a047e2a1-2dfd-3a66-b4e7-c0477ebf7d2c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Pacifist patriotism; the love of society as opposed to the love of the state."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "82b9a88e-d437-424a-a1c1-aea86d863d09",
                                "sense_id": "7f40aa4b-3091-3b80-a472-ad059412f890",
                                "text": "Matriotism is the opposite of patriotism. A yin to its yang, a counterforce to the violent militarism of patriotism. […] a Matriot would never send her child or another mother’s child to fight nonsense wars. She would march into war herself to protect her child from harm. […] Patriots cower behind the flag and send young people to die for the sake of material wealth."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b2f1337e-5670-32ab-b935-ccff504daeca",
                        "entry_id": "a047e2a1-2dfd-3a66-b4e7-c0477ebf7d2c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An enduring devotion to Mother Earth, ecology, sustainability, peace, and the survival of the human species."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
